+/* ============================================================
+   KnowDesign — design tokens
+
+   An additive layer: it only takes effect under html[data-brand="knowdesign"], so the
+   upstream token file (tokens.css) is untouched and Open Design builds are unchanged.
+   The attribute is set at runtime from the build profile.
+
+   Source of truth: the KnowMe desktop tokens (know-me-system, desktop/src/index.css at
+   commit 68f7ab8), decision D-005. Dark is KnowMe's native theme; light is its `body.light`
+   override. Where KnowMe has no step (a text tier between two of its colours, a hover
+   shade) the value is derived and marked "derived".
+
+   Mapping rule: neutrals carry the interface (--bg*, --text*, --accent*), exactly as upstream
+   uses them; ember takes the role upstream gives its green --brand, i.e. sparse emphasis.
+   Flat 2.0 (no strokes) is NOT applied here: it is an open design point to evaluate on real
+   screens before any wholesale change, so borders keep their upstream roles with KnowMe colours.
+
+   Selector order matters: the base block wins over upstream's :root by specificity, the
+   explicit dark block over [data-theme="dark"], and the media block over
+   html:not([data-theme]) in the OS-dark system mode.
+   ============================================================ */
+
+/* Light (also the base for both themes: theme-independent tokens live here once). */
+html[data-brand="knowdesign"] {
+  --bg: #f7f7f8;
+  --bg-app: #f7f7f8;
+  --bg-panel: #ffffff;
+  --bg-subtle: #f2f4f7;
+  --bg-muted: #e5e8ed;
+  --bg-elevated: #ffffff;
